d danny  bring the helios lander down for second  place and the unceremonious way they  plant their flag and the look on ed's  face does a great job to show you how  they feel about it there's a nice little  news section that lays out all of what's  happening now that the race is over even  though it was technically a tie the us  news considers it a win for the country  because it was their ship that got them  there now there's a race to find water  and helios has located some small  deposits which is enough for them to  start manufacturing their methane fuel  this is now in everyone's interest with  sojourner grounded phoenix will be  everyone's ride back to earth and they  need that methane since nasa uses  different fuel trying to cram eight  people into a hab with only enough  provisions for six makes things  difficult for the joint mission they  need to find water create their own  oxygen set up their nuclear power  generator grow their own food and even  though this all looks inspiring from  back on earth tensions are building  between the two crews fast it's cramped  hot they're rationing water and the  soviet commander seems committed to  challenging danielle every chance he  gets the one place where there's the  opposite of tension is between kelly and  alexei but that seems like it's probably  gonna cause some real problems later  things are going a little smoother at  heliospace but danny is still watching  ed's messages to karen he finds out that  he was the reason that ed decided to  abort their landing and that makes  things even more uncomfortable between  them as much as i haven't been enjoying  this story i do like how charged this  revelation is it stings because they  could have been first if ed had seen him  as a regular astronaut and now danny's  hearing that this guy who he resents  because of karen thinks of him as a son  this works a little better than danny  just wanting to be with karen and ed is  actively making things worse because  he's trying to do what he did with gordo  you can understand why ed is doing it  but we also know that it's a mistake we  see things start to bubble up when he  hurts his hand he gets an attitude when  ed tries to show concern and he gets his  hands on some tylenol with codeine that  we'll talk about again in a minute  in other not going to end well  developments margot contacts general  bradford about getting sergey's family  out in exchange for his defection she  doesn't mention him by name but assures  the now chairman of the joint chiefs  that he'll be a valuable asset to nasa  the mention of black ops makes this  sound like a very bad idea but i guess  it does make sense given her position i  don't love that it continues to be hard  to see how she gets out of this in fact  i really don't see it happening and i  also didn't love to see karen go back to  helios at first we do find out that that  was all set in motion by ross cosmos  reaching out to her and since it was  satisfying to see her turn the table  some on dev i guess that might turn out  alright i just don't see how her wanting  to start things from the ground up and  being good at it fits in here also i  don't know where it's heading but  they've been quietly introducing debs  partner richard hilliard last episode we  saw him looking at dev and mission  control after they aborted the landing  and here we see that there are some  tensions between them because mars is  costing so much money you get to know  the people at happy valley base through  a series of tv interviews they're  recording things get interesting when  will who's been inspired by their  monumental achievement comes out as gay  i think this works pretty well in that i  can see why he did it when he explains  his timing to danielle it absolutely  makes sense from his perspective plus  it's nice to see someone who's awed by  this experience of a brand new world at  the same time it creates problems so  when danielle doesn't react the way  you'd hoped she would that makes sense  too where it gets ugly is with his old  pal roland the soviet defector from last  season who he's been training with for  the last couple of years they've grown  close and now he doesn't want anything  to do with him he goes as far as going  to danielle and trying to get reassigned  which i don't know how he thought that  might turn out considering how many  people are there it's not necessarily  surprising to see someone have such a  negative reaction to homosexuality it's  ridiculous but there are a lot of  backward people out there ellen even  reminds us in this episode about deke's  negative reaction in season one it also  wasn't out of the ordinary for people to  be irrationally afraid of aids in the  early years though in our timeline it  seems like by 94 that wouldn't fly  danielle tells him that they all had hiv  tests on earth before they left but  doesn't say and besides you can't get  aids just by being next to someone i'm  not sure if the show is trying to point  out something about roland or if it's  trying to say that progress on people  knowing about aids is slower in this  reality either way his reaction is rough  to watch and will's announcement puts  ellen in a very difficult spot on the  one hand ellen and larry understand what  a psychological toll staying in the  closet can take on a person on the other  doing that has made it possible for them  to become the most powerful couple in  the world i suppose the show has made  the point that this power has its limits  and we see larry come up with a version  of don't ask don't tell to temporarily  solve their problem at the cost of it  not helping will at all knowing that  he'll be discharged from the army when  he returns what she calls uniforms first  is not a perfect solution in any  timeline but it does work for her  politically in this one on a personal  level it's not clear how she'll live  with the decision but that seems primed  to take a back seat to the other  incoming scandal that we learn about at  the end  karen helps the broker a deal with roz  cosmos who've discovered a large deposit  of liquid water the show never explains  why they were able to find this and nasa  wasn't but i guess we're just supposed  to accept that it sets up a situation  where helios and the soviets team up  behind nasa's back because ed is the one  who can get them there by helping them  helios will also benefit from this huge  discovery sergey comes through to tip  margot off about what's going on it's a  cute scene where at first i thought he  was betraying her installing a listening  device or something like that but it  turns out that he leaves an equation on  her record when she solves it she knows  what the secret mission is about and she  goes and tells elena she goes straight  to tell danielle which seemed a little  impulsive they had shown that she was  suspicious of the soviets in mission  control because of what she knows about  the engine but it was still a little  surprising that she just exposed what  they were doing like that i'm not sure  if this will come up again later but i  thought it was worth mentioning danielle  tells everyone else after ed's  well-intentioned thanksgiving party  turns into a brawl which i guess that  always happens no matter where you have  one of these things will finally calls  out roland for acting weird around him  and they do fight danielle finally lets  the soviet commander know what she  thinks and everyone in her crew is  pissed about the water ed tries to  smooth things over with kelly and she  talks him into bringing her along  because she thinks there's a good chance  there might be life in that water also  when he goes back to his hab he sends a  message to karen telling her that he's  worried about danny which of course gets  intercepted so danny has burnt through  his tylenol with codeine and he's gone  back and got some stronger oxycodone and  a little bit of speed to go along with  it they had a conversation where ed told  him that he would change the medical  protocol so he could stay on the planet  and this is another example of him  bending the rules so he can try to  recreate what he did with gordo when  he's talking to karen he tells her that  he's worried and you can imagine how  that might sit with the now loaded to  the gills danny who when he hears that  he thinks that he might not be cut out  for this starts punching the screen the  episode ends with ellen announcing her  new policy she confirms that it's too  late to help will in his situation on  the news you see it goes too far for  republicans and not far enough for  democrats which is something that they  expected larry's assistant is at a bar  talking to another gay friend or at  least someone pretending to be a friend  about this new policy and his  relationship with the first gentleman he  mentions that they've had relations in  the oval office that bring to mind the  real world monica lewinsky scandal on  his way out the friend gets a call and  tells the person on the other end that  he has to meet him in person to tell him  what he just found out it's not entirely  clear if it's his intention but it looks  like he'll end up exposing larry's  secret and that would put ellen in an  even tougher situation this was another  good episode character-wise it was great  will went from being the guy who was in  the right seat after the disaster to  someone who might turn out to be a  long-running character you care about it  will depend on what happens in the next  two years but i thought the actor did a  great job and really appreciated the  conversation he had with danielle even  though no one was satisfied in the end i  like that she says that reconstructing  the moral fabric of the universe is not  our mission when it might turn out doing  that anyway as i mentioned while i was  going through these things there were a  couple of details in the plot i didn't  think added up it wasn't enough to take  me out of it but i didn't find it as  easy to overlook these things as i think  they wanted us to we'll see how it all  plays out though the danny and ed thing  got a little more complicated but i feel  like they've passed the point where they  really have to come up with something  great to make it seem worth it after  dragging it out this long if the payoff  falls flat that'll be a big  disappointment i think it's clear larry  is going to be exposed but it kind of  makes my head spin when i try to think  of where it goes from there they're  obviously pulling from real world events  and bill clinton did survive his scandal  but this is a totally different case  based on her party affiliation i mean  right now we don't know of anything that  would make her lose the office but she  would become as powerless as it's  possible for a president to be and if  her vp's reaction to will is any  indication her party will be asking her  to resign what i liked about the episode  is it gave you a lot to think about and  it really drove home that idea that  everyone should be focused on what's  going on the struggle for survival the  opportunity to make something different  but that's not often how things really  work so i'm looking forward to see where  we go next and i think that's a good  place to leave things in the comments  tell me what you thought about new eden  and what you're hoping to see next week  please like this video if you enjoyed it  please subscribe to my channel if you  haven't already and thanks for watching  i'll talk to you soon

